    feat(runner): add sequential async write-queue primitive
    
    Proves D16's core claim (fan-out-parallel Epic 1): Node's single-threaded
    execution doesn't serialize concurrent async work by itself, since each
    await yields the event loop mid-transaction. write-queue.mjs is a PURE,
    store-agnostic FIFO queue that fully awaits each submitted transaction
    before starting the next, verified by a forced-interleaving test suite
    (concurrent multi-await transactions, staggered submission, and rejecting
    transactions that must not block/corrupt later ones).
    
    Registers the new file in docs/architecture-manifest.json (domain layer,
    alongside anti-loop.mjs) to keep the machine-checked architecture inventory
    test green.
    
    cell: fan-out-parallel-2
    
