    refactor(runner): thread async through dispatch/goal-check/merge/loop call chain
    
    Converts the runner pipeline from blocking spawnSync to async spawn end to
    end (spawnWorker, runGoalCheck, mergeRunnerItem, processItem, startupReap,
    runOnce, bin/fgos.mjs's runVerb, both CLI main()s) with zero observable
    behavior change -- still exactly one item dispatched at a time. Adds a
    dedicated goal-check.test.mjs (previously untested directly) and updates
    every existing call site across dispatch/goal-check/merge/loop/lock tests to
    await the now-async functions.
    
    Fixes a real timing bug found during conversion: resolving on the 'close'
    event (waits for stdio pipes to fully close) instead of 'exit' (fires once
    the process itself terminates) made a killed timeout silently wait out a
    still-running shell-forked grandchild -- switched both spawnWorker and
    runGoalCheck to 'exit', matching spawnSync's actual direct-child-only
    timeout semantics.
    
    fan-out-parallel-6
    
